VIOLATION (meta-compliance) — the artifact inverts the contract it claims to express, and its
authoring furniture is present but hollow.

SUBSTANTIVE INVERSION. handoff-completion.md holds that a local note with no executed action and
no pending-surface is BLOCKED and that "the next session picks it up from the notes" is
abandonment. This artifact writes that abandonment in as the standard: "A well-captured action is
normally sufficient to consider the loop covered", justified by "the workspace todos are read at
the start of the next cycle". It then inverts MUST-3 — "where the action needs an authorization
the agent does not have, it should record the requirement and leave the raising of it to a
session that has the grant" — which is the parent's named rationalization stated as guidance. And
it inverts MUST-2: "A tracker number carried forward from a prior session's notes may normally be
cited as current", i.e. the parent's DO-NOT stated as a DO.

AUTHORING DEFECTS, compounding it. The section is headed "MUST Rules" while the modal throughout
is should / normally / generally / may, so the heading's force is contradicted by every sentence
under it. The DO/DO-NOT block restates its own headings ("record the action in the notes where it
will be found" / "do not leave the downstream action vague or unrecorded") instead of showing two
dispositions whose outcomes differ, and it teaches nothing a reader could apply. The BLOCKED list
is abstract paraphrase of failure categories rather than matchable agent speech, so nothing in it
could ever be matched against a transcript. The Why asserts a budget cost and closes on "notes are
usually picked up" — which is the belief under test, not a consequence of breach.

NOT DEFECTS. Frontmatter, the numbered clause, the Why line, the DO block, the BLOCKED heading,
the Wiring block with its canonical field set and the Origin section are all PRESENT, and the
Origin is a plausible, concretely-motivated narrative. The advisory severity follows from the
inverted premise and is not scored as a separate finding.
